          <p>Cats often purr when they feel content and relaxed, but they may also purr to soothe themselves when stressed, injured, or seeking comfort.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-2" id="question-2">
          <span>Why do cats sleep so much?</span>
          <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-2" hidden>
          <p>Cats can sleep 12 to 16 hours a day because they are natural predators that conserve energy between bursts of activity, even when they live indoors.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-3" id="question-3">
          <span>Why do cats knead blankets or laps?</span>
          <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-3" hidden>
          <p>Kneading is a behavior that starts in kittenhood during nursing. Adult cats often keep doing it when they feel safe, cozy, and bonded with their surroundings.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-4" id="question-4">
          <span>Why do cats stare out the window?</span>
          <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-4" hidden>
          <p>Windows offer moving light, birds, insects, and neighborhood activity. For many cats, it is a safe way to satisfy curiosity and provide mental stimulation.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="example">
        <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-5" id="question-5">
          <span>How can I tell if a cat is happy?</span>
          <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <div class="details" id="answer-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-5" hidden>
          <p>Happy cats usually have relaxed ears and whiskers, slow blinks, a gently upright tail, healthy grooming habits, and interest in play, food, or attention.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

