 <!DOCTYPE html>
 <html lang="en">
 <head>
   <meta charset="UTF-8">
   <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
   <title>Cat FAQ</title>
   <style>
     :root {
       color-scheme: dark;
       --bg: #0b1020;
       --bg-accent: #11182b;
       --panel: #161f35;
       --panel-strong: #1d2945;
       --text: #f3f7ff;
       --muted: #b8c4e0;
       --border: #30405f;
       --accent: #88b4ff;
       --accent-strong: #a9c8ff;
       --shadow: 0 18px 45px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
     }

     * {
       box-sizing: border-box;
     }

     body {
       margin: 0;
       min-height: 100vh;
       font-family: Inter, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
       background:
         radial-gradient(circle at top, rgba(136, 180, 255, 0.16), transparent 32%),
         linear-gradient(180deg, var(--bg) 0%, #070b16 100%);
       color: var(--text);
       line-height: 1.6;
     }

     .skip-link {
       position: absolute;
       left: 1rem;
       top: 1rem;
       transform: translateY(-220%);
       padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
       border-radius: 0.75rem;
       background: var(--accent);
       color: #08101f;
       font-weight: 700;
       text-decoration: none;
       z-index: 10;
     }

     .skip-link:focus {
       transform: translateY(0);
       outline: 2px solid var(--text);
       outline-offset: 2px;
     }

     main {
       width: min(100%, 56rem);
       margin: 0 auto;
       padding: 4rem 1.25rem;
     }

     .hero {
       padding: 2rem 0 1rem;
     }

     h1 {
       margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
       font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
       line-height: 1.1;
       letter-spacing: -0.03em;
     }

     .intro {
       max-width: 42rem;
       margin: 0;
       color: var(--muted);
       font-size: 1.05rem;
     }

     .faq-list {
       display: grid;
       gap: 1rem;
       margin-top: 2rem;
     }

     .example {
       background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(29, 41, 69, 0.92), rgba(18, 27, 47, 0.96));
       border: 1px solid var(--border);
       border-radius: 1rem;
       box-shadow: var(--shadow);
       overflow: hidden;
     }

     .question {
       width: 100%;
       display: flex;
       align-items: center;
       justify-content: space-between;
       gap: 1rem;
       padding: 1.2rem 1.25rem;
       border: 0;
       background: transparent;
       color: var(--text);
       text-align: left;
       font: inherit;
       font-size: 1.05rem;
       font-weight: 700;
       cursor: pointer;
     }

     .question:hover {
       background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
     }

     .question:focus-visible {
       outline: 3px solid var(--accent);
       outline-offset: -3px;
     }

     .chevron {
       flex: 0 0 auto;
       width: 1rem;
       height: 1rem;
       border-right: 2px solid currentColor;
       border-bottom: 2px solid currentColor;
       transform: rotate(45deg);
       transition: transform 0.2s ease;
       color: var(--accent-strong);
       margin-right: 0.35rem;
     }

     .question[aria-expanded="true"] .chevron {
       transform: rotate(225deg);
     }

     .details {
       padding: 0 1.25rem 1.25rem;
       color: var(--muted);
     }

     .details p {
       margin: 0;
     }

     @media (max-width: 40rem) {
       main {
         padding: 3rem 1rem;
       }

       .question {
         align-items: flex-start;
       }
     }

     @media (forced-colors: active) {
       body {
         background: Canvas;
         color: CanvasText;
       }

       .example {
         background: Canvas;
         border-color: ButtonBorder;
         box-shadow: none;
       }

       .question {
         color: ButtonText;
       }

       .question:focus-visible,
       .skip-link:focus {
         outline-color: Highlight;
       }

       .details {
         color: CanvasText;
       }
     }
   </style>
 </head>
 <body>
   <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to main content</a>
   <main id="main-content">
     <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="page-title">
       <h1 id="page-title">Cat FAQ</h1>
       <p class="intro">
         Curious about cats? Browse quick answers to common questions about behavior,
         sleep, communication, and care.
       </p>
     </section>

     <section class="faq-list" aria-label="Frequently asked questions about cats">
       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-1" id="question-1">
           <span>Why do cats purr?</span>
           <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="answer-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-1" hidden>
           <p>Cats often purr when they feel content and relaxed, but they may also purr to soothe themselves when stressed, injured, or seeking comfort.</p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-2" id="question-2">
           <span>Why do cats sleep so much?</span>
           <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="answer-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-2" hidden>
           <p>Cats can sleep 12 to 16 hours a day because they are natural predators that conserve energy between bursts of activity, even when they live indoors.</p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-3" id="question-3">
           <span>Why do cats knead blankets or laps?</span>
           <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="answer-3" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-3" hidden>
           <p>Kneading is a behavior that starts in kittenhood during nursing. Adult cats often keep doing it when they feel safe, cozy, and bonded with their surroundings.</p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-4" id="question-4">
           <span>Why do cats stare out the window?</span>
           <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="answer-4" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-4" hidden>
           <p>Windows offer moving light, birds, insects, and neighborhood activity. For many cats, it is a safe way to satisfy curiosity and provide mental stimulation.</p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-5" id="question-5">
           <span>How can I tell if a cat is happy?</span>
           <span class="chevron" aria-hidden="true"></span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="answer-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="question-5" hidden>
           <p>Happy cats usually have relaxed ears and whiskers, slow blinks, a gently upright tail, healthy grooming habits, and interest in play, food, or attention.</p>
         </div>
       </div>
     </section>
   </main>

   <script>
     const questions = document.querySelectorAll(".question");

     questions.forEach((button) => {
       button.addEventListener("click", () => {
         const isExpanded = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";
         const details = document.getElementById(button.getAttribute("aria-controls"));

         button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isExpanded));
         details.hidden = isExpanded;
       });
     });
   </script>
 </body>
